# The image builds use the repo root as their build context, because chiron-base
# installs worker/ and stages worker/docker/patches/. Everything else in this
# repository is website source, and node_modules alone is 1.4 GB, so an
# unfiltered context would be sent to the daemon on every build.
#
# Allow-list rather than deny-list: exclude everything, then add back the one
# directory the Dockerfiles copy from. A new top-level directory is then excluded
# by default instead of silently joining the context.
*
!worker/
